    <div class="row">
        <div class="span12">
            <h3 class="headline">
                <span>pause (time in milliseconds) - Selenium IDE command</span>
            </h3>
        </div> 

        <div class="span12">

            <p>The  <span class="hired">pause</span> command is a simple wait command and useful to delay the execution of the automated testing
            for the specified time. Note that the wait time is in MILLIseconds. So if you want to wait for 3 seconds, enter 3000.</p>

            <p>Special feature: If you use <span class="hired">pause | 0</span> or
                simply <span class="hired">pause</span> without any number then the execution pauses until
                the user clicks the RESUME button.</br>
                <img src="~/Content/Images/pause0.webp"  alt="Pause 0 waits until RESUME is clicked" class="responsive-img">
            </p>
                <h3>Pause Example</h3>

            <p>In this example the Selenium IDE will wait for five seconds (5000ms).</p>
            <p>
                <table class="table table-bordered">
                    <thead>
                    <th class="col-md-2">Command</th>
                    <th class="col-md-5">Target</th>
                    <th class="col-md-5">Pattern/Text</th>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td>open</td>
                            <td>https://ui.vision/</td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="success">
                            <td>pause</td>
                            <td>5000</td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>open</td>
                            <td>https://ocr.space/</td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </p>

